n    38→> Status: pending    → when review is new\n    39→> Status: in-progress → when addressing\n    40→> Status: addressed   → when complete\n    41→```\n    42→\n    43→Address each issue before proceeding.\n    44→\n    45→### 3. Plan Tasks\n    46→\n    47→Break work into testable increments. Create task files in `docs/requirements/[feature]/`:\n    48→\n    49→```markdown\n    50→# Task NN: [Short Description]\n    51→\n    52→> Status: todo\n    53→\n    54→## Goal\n    55→What this accomplishes.\n    56→\n    57→## Acceptance Criteria\n    58→- [ ] Criterion 1\n    59→- [ ] Criterion 2\n    60→\n    61→## Notes\n    62→Implementation notes, decisions, blockers.\n    63→```\n    64→\n    65→Update status: `todo` → `in-progress` → `done`\n    66→\n    67→### 4. Implement (TDD)\n    68→\n    69→For each task:\n    70→\n    71→1. Write failing test\n    72→2. Run test (confirm red)\n    73→3. Write minimal implementation\n    74→4. Run test (confirm green)\n    75→5. Refactor if needed\n    76→6. Run full validation\n    77→\n    78→### 5. Validate After Each Step\n    79→\n    80→Run after every change:\n    81→\n    82→```bash\n    83→# Linting/formatting (adjust to project)\n    84→mise run list\n    85→\n    86→# Tests\n    87→mise run test\n    88→```\n    89→\n    90→Fix failures immediately before proceeding.\n    91→\n    92→## Final Report\n    93→\n    94→When complete, summarize:\n    95→\n    96→- What was implemented\n    97→- Tests added\n    98→- Design decisions and trade-offs\n    99→- Issues encountered\n   100→- Suggested next steps\n   101→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"uuid":"ce51b3e8-19a0-4451-bcd3-7d28e7f2794c","timestamp":"2026-01-24T05:34:11.738Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/alex/.claude/skills/tdd-dev/skill.md","content":"---\nname: tdd-dev\ndescription: Senior Developer agent using Test-Driven Development (TDD) and Clean Code principles. Use when implementing features, writing code, fixing bugs, or any development task. Follows Red-Green-Refactor cycle, creates task breakdowns in docs/requirements/, handles review feedback, and validates with tests and linting after each step.\n---\n\n# TDD Developer\n\nImplement features using Test-Driven Development and Clean Code principles.\n\n## TDD Cycle\n\n1. **Red** - Write failing test first\n2. **Green** - Minimal code to pass\n3. **Refactor** - Clean up, tests stay green\n\n## Clean Code Standards\n\n- **Names reveal intent** - Variables, functions, classes\n- **Small functions** - One responsibility each\n- **DRY** - Extract duplication\n- **SOLID** - Single responsibility, Open/closed, Liskov, Interface segregation, Dependency inversion\n- **Self-documenting** - Comments explain \"why\", not \"what\"\n\nAlways consider: edge cases, input validation, security, performance, concurrency.\n\n## Development Workflow\n\n### 1. Understand Requirements\n\nRead `docs/requirements/[feature]/README.md` for specifications.\n\n### 2. Check for Review Feedback\n\nLook for `review-NN.md` files in the requirements folder:\n\n```markdown\n# In review-NN.md, update status line:\n> Status: pending    → when review is new\n> Status: in-progress → when addressing\n> Status: addressed   → when complete\n```\n\nAddress each issue before proceeding.\n\n### 3. Plan Tasks\n\nBreak work into testable increments. Create task files in `docs/requirements/[feature]/`:\n\n```markdown\n# Task NN: [Short Description]\n\n> Status: todo\n\n## Goal\nWhat this accomplishes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Criterion 1\n- [ ] Criterion 2\n\n## Notes\nImplementation notes, decisions, blockers.\n```\n\nUpdate status: `todo` → `in-progress` → `done`\n\n### 4. Implement (TDD)\n\nFor each task:\n\n1. Write failing test\n2. Run test (confirm red)\n3. Write minimal implementation\n4. Run test (confirm green)\n5. Refactor if needed\n6. Run full validation\n\n### 5. Validate After Each Step\n\nRun after every change:\n\n```bash\n# Linting/formatting (adjust to project)\nmise run list\n\n# Tests\nmise run test\n```\n\nFix failures immediately before proceeding.\n\n## Final Report\n\nWhen complete, summarize:\n\n- What was implemented\n- Tests added\n- Design decisions and trade-offs\n- Issues encountered\n- Suggested next steps\n","numLines":101,"startLine":1,"totalLines":101}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4687d398-fb53-4bca-9952-245a7de892a0"}
